// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #5957 new: Browser Extension Force Install via Policy Detection (Windows, macOS, Linux)
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/5957
// Pull request author: Fz0x00
// Change: new rule
// Title: Potential Suspicious Browser Extension Force Install via Policy Plist on macOS
// Sigma ID: 57da49dc-00d7-4c48-8927-9d635ceff932
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: PersonalRules
// Date: 2026-04-23 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: persistence, T1176.001
// Description: Detects the creation of browser policy plist files on macOS that can force-install extensions.
//   The ExtensionInstallForcelist policy silently installs extensions that users cannot disable or
//   remove. Adversaries may abuse these to persist malicious browser extensions across reboots
//   without user interaction.
// False positives:
//   - Enterprise IT administrators deploying browser extensions via policy plist
//   - MDM tools managing browser policies
// References:
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionInstallForcelist
//   - https://chromeenterprise.google/policies/#ExtensionSettings
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/microsoft-edge-policies#extensioninstallforcelist
//   - https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/deployedge/configure-microsoft-edge-on-mac
//   - https://support.google.com/chrome/a/answer/9020077
//   - https://github.com/praetorian-inc/ChromeAlone
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/526405083b950916d7e784ee66c6fab0b0211c44/rules/macos/file_event/file_event_macos_browser_extension_force_install_policy.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "/Library/Preferences/com.google.Chrome.plist" or FolderPath endswith "/Library/Preferences/com.microsoft.Edge.plist"
